.TH "tclsimrawreader" 3tcl 0\&.5 "tclsimrawreader" "Tcl tclsimrawreader package"
.SH NAME
tclsimrawreader - Commands in namespace tclsimrawreader
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?option?\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBopenraw\fP \fI?-dialect name? ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-namespace name? filepath\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE\fP \fIsubcommand \&.\&.\&.\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE close\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE header\fP \fI?-plot index?\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE names\fP \fI?-plot index?\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE npoints\fP \fI?-plot index?\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE plots\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE vector\fP \fI?-plot index? name ?-from index? ?-count index? ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-name destination|#auto? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBRAWFILE vectors\fP \fI?-plot index? -all|namesList ?-from index? ?-count index? ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-names dictionary|#auto? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
.SH ::TCLSIMRAWREADER
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBconfigure\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Queries or changes package-wide representation and collision defaults in this Tcl interpreter\&.
.RS 4n
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?option?\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists policy
Default destination collision policy: error or replace; initially error\&.
.TP
-output mode
Default output representation: list or vector; initially list\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
With no arguments, returns all settings as an option/value dictionary\&. With one option, returns its value\&.
With option/value pairs, validates all settings before applying them and returns the complete configuration\&.
Invalid options or values, or unavailable RBC support leave the configuration unchanged\&. Selecting
vector mode requires an RBC-enabled build and a loadable rbc::vector package; list queries/settings do not
load RBC\&. Defaults are independent in separate interpreters\&.
.PP
New raw-file handles capture these defaults unless -output or -ifexists is supplied explicitly at creation\&.
Existing handles retain their settings\&. Per-read overrides take precedence over the handle default\&.
This public command is not namespace-exported; call it as ::tclsimrawreader::configure\&.
The collision policy affects vector output only; it can be configured while using list mode or without RBC\&.
Replacement still requires a compatible, writable destination\&. Namespace selection and naming are unchanged\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set saved [::tclsimrawreader::configure]
::tclsimrawreader::configure -output vector -ifexists replace
::tclsimrawreader::configure -output
::tclsimrawreader::configure {*}$saved
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
selected option value for a single-option query; otherwise all settings as a dictionary\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBopenraw\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Open channel to provided \&.raw file, creates subcommand, parses header(s) information from the file\&.
Every ::tclsimrawreader::openraw returns a command (e\&.g\&. ::tclsimrawreader::s1)\&. The following
subcommands operate on that file instance\&.
.RS 4n
\fBopenraw\fP \fI?-dialect name? ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-namespace name? filepath\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-dialect name
Optional dialect, possible values are generic and ltspice, default is generic
.TP
-ifexists policy
Default collision policy, error or replace; inherits the package configuration (initially error)
.TP
-namespace name
Fixed destination namespace for all vector output; created with missing parents at open\&.
.TP
-output mode
Default output, list or vector; inherits the package configuration (initially list)
.TP
filepath
Path to SPICE \&.raw file\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Relative namespace names resolve against the caller opening the handle\&. Empty names are rejected\&. If omitted,
vector destinations continue to use the namespace calling each read\&. Closing the handle does not delete the
namespace or output RBC vectors\&. The option also works with list defaults and later vector overrides\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set rawfile [tclsimrawreader::openraw /path/to/ac\&.raw]
set rawfile [tclsimrawreader::openraw /path/to/ac\&.raw -output vector -ifexists replace]
set rawfile [tclsimrawreader::openraw -dialect ltspice /path/to/ac\&.raw]
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
command name to work with the file, references as RAWFILE later
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
A
command
ensemble\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE\fP \fIsubcommand \&.\&.\&.\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The ensemble supports the following subcommands:
.RS 4n
.TP
\fIclose\fP
Closes channel to provided \&.raw file and deletes subcommand\&.
.TP
\fIheader\fP
Gets dictionary containing metadata from the header for the selected plot\&. If provided without -plot option, returns header from the first plot\&.
.TP
\fInames\fP
Gets list of vectors' (variables') names defined in the header\&. If provided without -plot option, returns names from the first plot\&.
.TP
\fInpoints\fP
Returns the number of points in the selected plot\&.
.TP
\fIplots\fP
Gets list of dictionaries containing information about the plots in the \&.raw file\&.
.TP
\fIvector\fP
Gets the values of specified vector (variable) for selected plot, in certain range if specified\&. If plot index is not provided, return values from the first plot\&.
.TP
\fIvectors\fP
Gets the values of specified vectors (variables) for selected plot (or all vectors), in certain range if specified\&. If plot index is not provided, return values from the first plot\&.
.RE
.PP
Refer to the documentation of each subcommand for details\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE close\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Closes channel to provided \&.raw file and deletes subcommand\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE close\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$rawfile close
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP close\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE header\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Gets dictionary containing metadata from the header for the selected plot\&. If provided without -plot
option, returns header from the first plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE header\fP \fI?-plot index?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-plot index
Index of the plot, optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Result dictionary containing next keys:
.TP
\(bu
title - string from Title: header field
.TP
\(bu
date - string from Date: header field
.TP
\(bu
plotname - string from Plotname: header field
.TP
\(bu
nvariables - string from No\&. Variables: header field
.TP
\(bu
npoints - string from No\&. Points: header field
.TP
\(bu
pointstride - number of bytes occupied by a single point
.TP
\(bu
flags - list of flags from Flags: header field
.TP
\(bu
variables - list of dictionaries containing information from Variables: header block and derived data
.PP
Each variable key value contains dictionary with keys:
.TP
\(bu
index - variable index
.TP
\(bu
name - name of the variable
.TP
\(bu
type - type of variable
.TP
\(bu
storage - string characterising the storage of the value for variable, real32 = 4 bytes, real64 = 8 bytes, complex128 = 16 bytes
.TP
\(bu
valuebytes - number of bytes per value
.TP
\(bu
offsetbytes - number of bytes from the start of point memory block to the start of variable value
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$rawfile header
$rawfile header -plot 1
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP header\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE names\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Gets list of vectors' (variables') names defined in the header\&. If provided without -plot option, returns
names from the first plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE names\fP \fI?-plot index?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-plot index
Index of the plot, optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$rawfile names
$rawfile names -plot 1
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP names\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE npoints\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Returns the number of points in the selected plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE npoints\fP \fI?-plot index?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-plot index
Zero-based plot index; defaults to zero\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP npoints\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Returns the number of points in the selected plot\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE plots\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Gets list of dictionaries containing information about the plots in the \&.raw file\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE plots\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Each dictionary contains next keys:
.TP
\(bu
index - index of the plot, starting with 0
.TP
\(bu
kind - format of the data, either binary or ASCII
.TP
\(bu
title - string from Title: plot's header field
.TP
\(bu
plotname - string from Plotname: plot's header field
.TP
\(bu
nvariables - string from No\&. Variables: plot's header field
.TP
\(bu
npoints - string from No\&. Points: plot's header field
.TP
\(bu
dataoffset - number of bytes immediately after Binary:/Values: marker line for plot
.TP
\(bu
databytes - number of bytes occupied by a data block of the plot
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP plots\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list of dictionaries
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE vector\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Gets the values of specified vector (variable) for selected plot, in certain range if specified\&. If plot
index is not provided, return values from the first plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE vector\fP \fI?-plot index? name ?-from index? ?-count index? ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-name destination|#auto? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-count index
Number of values from the number provided by -from, or from the start otherwise, optional, integer\&.
.TP
-from index
Number of the values from the start of the vector, optional, integer\&.
.TP
-ifexists policy
Override collision handling for this call: error or replace
.TP
-name destination
Explicit output name or #auto for a fresh RBC-generated name; vector output only\&.
.TP
-namespace name
Destination override for this read; vector output only, relative to the caller, created if missing\&.
.TP
-output mode
Override the handle output for this call: list or vector
.TP
-plot index
Index of the plot, optional\&.
.TP
name
Name of the vector (variable)
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
In vector mode, safe literal names (including v(out) and v(1)) are preserved and qualified in the handle
namespace, if configured, or the calling namespace otherwise\&. A per-call -namespace takes
precedence\&. Unsupported/namespace-bearing names and names beginning with the reserved _raw_ prefix become
_raw_ plus uppercase hexadecimal UTF-8 bytes\&. Original dictionary keys are unchanged\&. Requires RBC's -literal
true creation support\&. New vectors have no mapped arrays and outlive the handle\&. Complex raw data creates complex
RBC vectors\&. Replacement preserves same-type vector identity; an unrelated command or a numeric type mismatch is
an error\&. See the start page for naming and ownership\&. Relative -namespace resolves against the read caller and
creates missing parents\&.  Empty namespaces are rejected\&. Fully qualified destinations override -namespace; their
parent must exist\&.  RBC expands a final #auto component in the selected namespace\&. Overrides do not change handle
defaults\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$rawfile vector -plot 2 ID(M1)
$rawfile vector -plot 2 ID(M1) -from 5 -count 16
$rawfile vector ID(M1) -from 5
$rawfile vector ID(M1) -count 16
$rawfile vector ID(M1)
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP vector\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list of values in list mode, or fully qualified RBC vector command name in vector mode
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBRAWFILE vectors\fR (::tclsimrawreader)
.RE
.PP
Gets the values of specified vectors (variables) for selected plot (or all vectors), in certain range
if specified\&. If plot index is not provided, return values from the first plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBRAWFILE vectors\fP \fI?-plot index? -all|namesList ?-from index? ?-count index? ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-names dictionary|#auto? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-all|namesList
List of vectors' (variables') names, or -all to read all availible vectors\&.
.TP
-count index
Number of values from the number provided by -from, or from the start otherwise, optional, integer\&.
.TP
-from index
Number of the values from the start of the vector, optional, integer\&.
.TP
-ifexists policy
Override collision handling for this call: error or replace
.TP
-names destinations
#auto for all selected signals, or a raw-name-to-destination dictionary; vector output only\&.
.TP
-namespace name
Destination override for this read; vector output only, relative to the caller, created if missing\&.
.TP
-output mode
Override the handle output for this call: list or vector
.TP
-plot index
Index of the plot, optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Options do not change the handle defaults\&. Vector naming, types, collision handling and ownership follow the
single-vector command\&. Relative -namespace resolves against the read caller and creates missing parents\&. Empty
namespaces are rejected\&. Fully qualified destinations override -namespace; their parent must exist\&. RBC expands
a final #auto component in the selected namespace\&. All selected data is decoded before any destination data is
replaced\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$rawfile vectors -plot 2 {ID(M1) V(VD)}
$rawfile vectors -plot 2 {ID(M1) V(VD)} -from 5 -count 16
$rawfile vectors {ID(M1) V(VD)} -from 5
$rawfile vectors {ID(M1) V(VD)} -count 16
$rawfile vectors {ID(M1) V(VD)}
$rawfile vectors -plot 2 -all
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP vectors\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary of original raw names to value lists, or to fully qualified RBC vectors' commands' names


.SH SEE ALSO
tclsimrawreader(n) - package's main page
.br
tclsimrawreader-notes-and-internals(n) - information about implementation
.br
.sp 1
